<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 07:26:15 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>US military cloud platform reportedly hacked as Pentagon insists systems are secure</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261128-us-military-cloud-platform-reportedly-hacked-as-pentagon-insists-systems-are-secure</link><description>
Hackers reportedly breached the US Air Force's Cloud One platform late Friday, potentially exposing sensitive military data. The Pentagon did not specifically deny that the system had been accessed, but insists its networks remain secure amid an ongoing spate of cyber-related data incidents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d18578fc-eaf0-11f1-9279-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-27T110013Z-410933699-RC2K8OA5ONF8-RTRMADP-3-USA-PENTAGON-AIR-FORCE-CLOUD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d18578fc-eaf0-11f1-9279-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-27T110013Z-410933699-RC2K8OA5ONF8-RTRMADP-3-USA-PENTAGON-AIR-FORCE-CLOUD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33866d7c-eaf1-11f1-ab33-b7f3664ca006</guid><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 06:04:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d18578fc-eaf0-11f1-9279-f9cf020caef6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-27T110013Z-410933699-RC2K8OA5ONF8-RTRMADP-3-USA-PENTAGON-AIR-FORCE-CLOUD.jpg">© Dado Ruvic, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Back to Black Friday: 'We are now bombarded with offers throughout the year'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261127-black-friday-how-the-global-shopping-phenomenon-is-evolving-amid-the-cost-of-living-crisis</link><description>
Black Friday was once a single day of holiday sales, held the day after Thanksgiving. Then retailers began kicking things off a day early, on Thanksgiving itself. “We are now bombarded with offers throughout the year,” says Hilary Ingham, Professor of Economics and Department Head at Lancaster University, who has no plans to shop this Black Friday. Ingham acknowledges a growing sense of “retail fatigue” but still sees the potential for a peak in sales. Meanwhile, an investigation by The Telegraph suggests that six in ten of the most popular products were actually more expensive than earlier in the year, underscoring the need for consumers to remain vigilant and track prices over time.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57189f3a-ea74-11f1-8b39-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261127-131851-132536-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57189f3a-ea74-11f1-8b39-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261127-131851-132536-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5c3aa9ae-ea74-11f1-ad93-d5f2fc6d09a7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:53:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Almost a million Americans left without power on Thanksgiving as storm sweeps East Coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261127-almost-a-million-americans-left-without-power-on-thanksgiving-as-storm-sweeps-east-coast</link><description>
Nearly a million people were left without power Thursday after a severe storm lashed the East Coast of the US, tearing up trees and powerlines on Thanksgiving. New York City authorities had been forced to postpone the annual Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade due to the intense winds.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c6bc3aa-e9e5-11f1-8f2f-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/ccf7f65a00f29aabccd88a0ab76a7d977ca3bffb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c6bc3aa-e9e5-11f1-8f2f-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/ccf7f65a00f29aabccd88a0ab76a7d977ca3bffb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a4194fe0-ea2f-11f1-8863-59fe6fdc8cf5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:14:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c6bc3aa-e9e5-11f1-8f2f-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/ccf7f65a00f29aabccd88a0ab76a7d977ca3bffb.jpg">© Kena Betancur, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In California, exceptional tides and nearly 9m-high waves batter the coast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261126-in-california-exceptional-tides-and-nearly-9m-high-waves-batter-the-coast</link><description>
USA: Powerful waves and king tides destroyed part of a pier in Pacifica, south of San Francisco, on Wednesday. In Marin County, authorities issued a temporary evacuation order and urged people to stay away from the beach. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3da49d80-e9af-11f1-b62c-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/CALIFORNIA-Minia.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3da49d80-e9af-11f1-b62c-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/CALIFORNIA-Minia.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6775884a-e9af-11f1-9f80-5fc06f4e7cce</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:01:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Unacceptable': China, EU among major economies against new US tariffs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-unacceptable-major-economies-push-back-against-new-us-tariffs</link><description>
China, the European Union and other major trading partners on Thursday criticised new US tariffs of up to 20 percent proposed by US President Donald Trump after a probe into alleged global overcapacity, raising the prospect of fresh trade tensions with allies and rivals alike.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b38f54e-e968-11f1-b414-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T135439Z-2052634195-RC21VOAE4UVU-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-TARIFFS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b38f54e-e968-11f1-b414-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T135439Z-2052634195-RC21VOAE4UVU-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-TARIFFS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f00084ba-e966-11f1-9d8b-3b869f56b586</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:16:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b38f54e-e968-11f1-b414-81bc2b1dcd65/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-25T135439Z-2052634195-RC21VOAE4UVU-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-TARIFFS.jpg">© Dado Ruvic, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Powerful US storm forces historic postponement of New York's Thanksgiving Day Parade</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261126-powerful-us-storm-forces-historic-postponement-of-thanksgiving-day-parade-in-new-york</link><description>
A powerful storm forecast to bring fierce winds and heavy rain to the northeastern United States has forced the unprecedented postponement of the city's 100th annual Thanksgiving Day Parade, with the event rescheduled for Saturday. Officials warned that Thursday's conditions could bring down tree limbs and power lines, while posing a safety risk to the parade's giant balloons and the crowds below.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1a0cb74-e935-11f1-813e-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329715905101.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1a0cb74-e935-11f1-813e-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329715905101.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41965f6a-e936-11f1-8632-13afe90628d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:11:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1a0cb74-e935-11f1-813e-c131ae9bfe9c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26329715905101.jpg">© Yuki Iwamura, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>New US tariffs: 'Trump lashing out really indiscriminately', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261125-new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says</link><description>
The United States on Wednesday unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5fbaf158-e987-11f1-86c8-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e048ab4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5fbaf158-e987-11f1-86c8-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e048ab4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7187f4d6-e91d-11f1-a3c9-152d2507c1bd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:13:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New US tariffs: 'Trump lashing out really indiscriminately', expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/new-us-tariffs-trump-lashing-out-really-indiscriminately-expert-says</link><description>
The United States on Wednesday unveiled proposed tariffs on 14 economies including the European Union and China, after a months-long probe into alleged excess production. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Dean Baker, senior economist at the Centre for Economic and Policy Research, says that "there has to be some mechanism for better coordinating China's involvement in the world trade system and ideally the US, the EU, Canada would have a common front, some clear ground rules that we could agree to, that China could agree to, to be mutually beneficial. It's not a step in that direction, we have President Trump lashing out really indiscriminately. It's very hard to see his approach being very productive".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5fbaf158-e987-11f1-86c8-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e048ab4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5fbaf158-e987-11f1-86c8-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5e048ab4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">755e49e4-e91c-11f1-9b50-6922dcda68b9</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:11:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Army detonates lead explosives in Iowa despite contamination fears</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-us-army-detonates-lead-explosives-iowa-despite-community-backlash</link><description>
The US Army on Wednesday blew up 5 tons of lead-based explosives at an ammunition plant in Iowa despite community backlash over fears of environmental contamination. The detonation was postponed three times, but got the green light after a federal appeals court this week found the US Environmental Protection Agency adequately incorporated safeguards to minimise the dispersal of lead dust.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d87f18b0-e8e4-11f1-9b78-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2306835116.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d87f18b0-e8e4-11f1-9b78-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2306835116.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a168b0a-e8e5-11f1-b6fd-fd093e838723</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:08:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d87f18b0-e8e4-11f1-9b78-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2306835116.jpg">© Scott Olson, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'We need to stop the war in Iran': US Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261125-we-need-to-stop-the-war-in-iran-us-congresswoman-pramila-jayapal</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Democratic Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal laid out her priorities for the new Congress: ending the war in Iran, tackling the cost-of-living crisis, curbing political corruption and holding the Trump administration accountable for its immigration crackdown. She also called for the "complete" dismantling of the US federal immigration agency ICE and backed an end to US military funding for Israel.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fdce0e-e8c0-11f1-b0b2-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/pramila.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fdce0e-e8c0-11f1-b0b2-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/pramila.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cd7768a0-e8bc-11f1-87c7-dfbe018349b6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:46:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump announces new tariffs on EU, China despite US midterms defeat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-trump-announces-new-tariffs-eu-china-despite-us-midterms-defeat</link><description>
President Donald Trump's administration on Wednesday reignited global trade tensions by proposing new tariffs on some of the largest US trading partners, including the EU, Japan and Taiwan. China could be slapped with a 20 percent tariff, a senior official said. The announcement came weeks after a cost-of-living crisis landed the Republicans a sweeping defeat in the US midterms.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/799ca916-e47f-11f1-a351-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T200647Z-677358732-RC2LKOAOVK5M-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-NEW-YORK-TIMES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/799ca916-e47f-11f1-a351-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T200647Z-677358732-RC2LKOAOVK5M-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-NEW-YORK-TIMES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">265988ea-e8d6-11f1-b4c8-a109eb9db9aa</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:38:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/799ca916-e47f-11f1-a351-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T200647Z-677358732-RC2LKOAOVK5M-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-NEW-YORK-TIMES.jpg">© Aaron Schwartz, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Cyberattack exposes unclassified information from CIA system, US media reports</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261125-cyberattack-exposes-unclassified-information-from-cia-system-us-media-reports</link><description>
A recently discovered hack on a CIA analysis system exposed some unclassified information, US media reported on Tuesday. The breach is the latest in a series of cyber attacks that have targeted US government departments and major companies in recent weeks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a246fea-e8bc-11f1-9c05-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-24T215637Z-1247257564-RC2ONW92JHR0-RTRMADP-3-CYBERSECURITY-USA-BREACH.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a246fea-e8bc-11f1-9c05-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-24T215637Z-1247257564-RC2ONW92JHR0-RTRMADP-3-CYBERSECURITY-USA-BREACH.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42f3e8ba-e8bd-11f1-a31f-0f9e6db4c61c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:48:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2a246fea-e8bc-11f1-9c05-29d00e23de9a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-24T215637Z-1247257564-RC2ONW92JHR0-RTRMADP-3-CYBERSECURITY-USA-BREACH.jpg">© Evelyn Hockstein, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>New York jury convicts Huawei of stealing trade secrets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261124-new-york-jury-convicts-huawei-of-stealing-trade-secrets</link><description>
A New York jury on Tuesday found Chinese telecom giant Huawei guilty of stealing trade secrets and other criminal offences, but acquitted it of a racketeering conspiracy and obstruction of justice. The verdict followed a three-month trial in New York in a case that adds to longstanding US efforts to curb Huawei's operations over alleged threats to national security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f80d975e-e85a-11f1-a844-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/7864970837c55973feb3edee9f03ff64d29f452b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f80d975e-e85a-11f1-a844-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/7864970837c55973feb3edee9f03ff64d29f452b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28dfdd66-e85f-11f1-839b-41fb5aa200ac</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:31:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f80d975e-e85a-11f1-a844-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/7864970837c55973feb3edee9f03ff64d29f452b.jpg">© Josep Lago, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tech executives' investment in Trump 'clearly paying off' as Huang reinstated at Nvidia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tech-executives-investment-in-trump-clearly-paying-off-as-huang-reinstated-at-nvidia</link><description>
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, The Hill Senior Technology Reporter Miranda Nazzaro says that the reinstatement of Jensen Huang at Nvidia represents "the culmination of a two-year push of tech executives to get closer to President Trump and their investment in the president is clearly paying off".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4055be64-e8bb-11f1-bafb-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2e663a00.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4055be64-e8bb-11f1-bafb-1991d4929b54/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2e663a00.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bdf9ec88-e851-11f1-9638-53e0f86e68d6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:57:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Quid pro quo’: Nvidia too big to fail or ‘too close to personal interest of people around Trump’?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/quid-pro-quo-nvidia-too-big-to-fail-or-too-close-to-personal-interest-of-people-around-trump</link><description>
Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Bernard Benhamou, Secretary General of the Institute of Digital Sovereignty and Senior Lecturer in Internet Governance at Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne University. What does Jensen Huang's return to Nvidia mean for Trump, Lutnick, the US, the AI industry and China? Describing Huang as “the global banker of the AI industry”, Benhamou explains: “He is the visionary, he is the banker. He's not only the chip maker.” He also warns of the repercussions of Donald Trump's decision to reinstate the Nvidia CEO, with congressional and judicial scrutiny looming. “It's far from over. It's just the beginning.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14848588-e841-11f1-b3f2-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-150347-151420-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14848588-e841-11f1-b3f2-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261124-150347-151420-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">19db41e8-e841-11f1-bbc6-bf188522b68b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:43:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Jensen Huang's Nvidia comeback sends AI videos into overdrive</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261124-jensen-huang-s-nvidia-comeback-sends-ai-videos-into-overdrive</link><description>
Just 11 days after resigning as Nvidia CEO, Jensen Huang's return has unleashed a fresh wave of AI-generated videos. But the internet has changed its tune: while last week's memes mocked Huang, many now celebrate his comeback. One viral video purportedly showing him dancing is actually AI-manipulated footage of a basketball coach from 2016. From humiliation to hero worship, the technology Nvidia helped popularise is rewriting the narrative surrounding its own CEO, as Vedika Bahl explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2eb920c-e84d-11f1-917f-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/nvidia-return.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2eb920c-e84d-11f1-917f-81da3ab2acbb/w:1024/p:16x9/nvidia-return.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">02b482e2-e84e-11f1-8729-3d8bb363777f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:28:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Did Nvidia knowingly send chips to China 'cutout'? Was there 'pay-to-play' involving Trump, Lutnick?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261124-did-nvidia-knowingly-send-chips-to-china-cutout-was-there-pay-to-play-involving-trump-lutnick</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Professor of Practice at NYU School of Law and a former federal prosecutor known for leading major Department of Justice (DOJ) and FBI investigations. Professor Weissmann joins us to discuss the legal and ethical questions surrounding the Trump administration's dealings with chipmaker Nvidia following the reinstatement of Jensen Huang as president and CEO.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53781c42-e8bd-11f1-bfcf-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-59d06647.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53781c42-e8bd-11f1-bfcf-95e072ff0a91/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-59d06647.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e1c95450-e84c-11f1-be3c-2fc567fd097a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:20:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>The Bukele method: Will Salvadoran leader's strong-arm tactics work for Haiti?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261124-the-bukele-method-will-salvadoran-leader-s-strong-arm-tactics-work-for-haiti</link><description>
Haitians are hailing the Bukele method. Citizens of the Americas' poorest nation are cheering the Salvadoran president’s "shoot first, ask questions later" method of dealing with the gangs that have overrun their country for the past six years. Can the police force deployed actually restore law and order? We ask about the latest in a decades-long list of efforts by the international community to support Haiti.
